    "sources": [
      "USB HID Usage Tables 1.4: Keyboard/Keypad page (0x07) and Consumer page (0x0C)",
      "Hubbo's HID descriptor (firmware/src/ble_hid.cpp): keyboard usages up to 0x65, consumer up to 0x3FF"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "For any host that takes a standard keyboard: a PC, a Mac, a Linux box running Kodi, a browser.",
      "Navigation uses the keyboard's arrow keys, Enter for Select and Escape for Back. Menu is the Application (context menu) key.",
      "Letters are KeyA-KeyZ and the Home/End keys are KeyHome/KeyEnd, so they don't clash with remote names like Home or the A-D buttons on some remotes.",
      "Media keys are on the Consumer page; most desktop systems honour them.",
      "No modifiers (Ctrl, Alt, Shift) in this version, and no power control."
    ],
    "verify": [
      "key_delay_ms 50 is a guess; a keyboard host needs no real gap"
    ]
  }
